\name{MathTransforms}
\alias{MathTransforms}
\title{Element-by-element mathematical functions an instrument applies to one candle column}
\description{
Each method fetches the instrument's candles through \code{prices()}, adds one column and returns the candles. The class is a link in the chain of analysis classes that \code{Instrument} inherits, and \code{Instrument} supplies \code{prices()}.

The \code{talib} package has no math transforms, so each is computed with the base R function that TA-Lib's C code calls, such as \code{acos()} for TA-Lib's \code{ACOS}. TA-Lib's math transforms need no earlier candles, so every row gets a value.
}
